# Flavor text for found documents turned up by asteroid/debris salvage loot.

asteroid-found-document-logbook = The handwriting gets worse toward the bottom of the page.
    "Day 9 out past the beacon. Vein's richer than the survey said, but the rock keeps shifting - something's knocking loose further in than we've drilled. Took two crates back to the shuttle today, left the rest marked. If the relief crew reads this: don't trust the depth gauge, it's been lying to us for a week."

asteroid-found-document-claim = The ink has smeared, but the signature block is still legible.
    "Claim filed on this rock by right of first drill, no exceptions, no partners. Anyone caught siphoning from this vein will answer to the company arbitrator, assuming they can find one all the way out here. Found gold? Good for you. Still mine."

asteroid-found-document-manifest = Most of the manifest is crossed out in heavy pencil.
    "Water, rations, spare filters, three crates of fuel - struck through, struck through, struck through. Only one line is left untouched at the bottom: 'bring the good drill this time.' Whoever wrote it apparently never got the chance."
